---
import Main from "@/layouts/Main.astro";
import { siteSettings } from "@/config/siteSettings";

const siteName = siteSettings.branding.siteName;
---

<Main title={`About | ${siteName}`}>
  <section class="prose" data-bible-autolink>
    <h1>About {siteName}</h1>

    <blockquote>
      <p>&ldquo;Freely you have received; freely give.&rdquo;</p>
      <p><cite>&mdash; Matthew 10:8</cite></p>
    </blockquote>

    <p>
      <em>Dorean</em> is the Greek word Jesus used when He sent out the twelve: what they had received
      without cost, they were to give without cost. It is the same word Paul uses for our justification,
      &ldquo;freely by His grace&rdquo; (Romans 3:24), and the same word in the last invitation of the
      Bible: &ldquo;let the one who is thirsty come, and the one who desires the water of life drink freely&rdquo;
      (Revelation 22:17).
    </p>

    <p>
      {siteName} asks and answers the questions Christians raise when they meet that command: what it
      means, how it fits with paying pastors, and what it says about selling sermons, books, Bible translations,
      worship songs, conferences, seminary courses and counseling. The short version, which the rest of
      the site unfolds, is this: <strong>ministry should be supported, not sold.</strong>
    </p>

    <h2>How to use this site</h2>

    <ul>
      <li>Each answer is short, with the Scripture that grounds it listed underneath.</li>
      <li>
        Most questions also have a fuller explanation. Open &ldquo;Read the full explanation&rdquo;
        under the answer.
      </li>
      <li>Hover over or tap any Scripture reference to read the verse (Berean Standard Bible).</li>
      <li>Browse by category, search, or start with the first question and go in order.</li>
    </ul>

    <h2>Where this comes from</h2>

    <p>
      The argument here owes most to Conley Owens&apos;s book
      <a href="https://thedoreanprinciple.org" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer"
        ><em>The Dorean Principle</em></a
      >, which is free to read online and dedicated to the public domain, and to the articles at
      <a href="https://sellingjesus.org" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Selling Jesus</a
      >. The questions and answers on this site are a fresh summary in question-and-answer form, so
      that the case can be read a piece at a time and taught.
    </p>

    <p>
      The answers were drafted with the help of AI for Michael Coughlin to review, and are marked as
      such. Weigh every answer against the Scripture cited under it, as the Bereans did (Acts
      17:11).
    </p>

    <h2>A word of charity</h2>

    <p>
      Many faithful ministers charge for their work because that is how the work was handed to them,
      not because they love money. This site is written to persuade brothers and sisters, not to
      accuse them. &ldquo;What then is the issue? Just this: that in every way, whether by false
      motives or true, Christ is preached. And in this I rejoice&rdquo; (Philippians 1:18).
    </p>
  </section>
</Main>
